From 3cc802253a2bfcce3fb470c2069760cf35e85850 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicolas Graves <ngraves@ngraves.fr>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 20:15:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] scanner: wrap client event objects with their declared type

Object arguments in client events were wrapped with the event emitter's
interface type.  For example, wl_surface.enter's wl_output argument became a
<wl-surface> containing the output proxy address.  Besides exposing the wrong
API type, unwrapping it through unwrap-wl-output consequently failed.

Use the object argument's interface metadata when generating its wrapper, as
is already done for typed new_id request results.  Preserve the existing
emitter-type fallback for object arguments that declare no interface.
---
 modules/wayland/scanner.scm | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/modules/wayland/scanner.scm b/modules/wayland/scanner.scm
index 793b069..05f212e 100644
--- a/modules/wayland/scanner.scm
+++ b/modules/wayland/scanner.scm
@@ -344,6 +344,8 @@
                                                        #`((ffi:pointer->string name*)))
                                                        ((equal? atype "object")
-                                                        #`((#,(->syntax (make-%wrap-name iname))
+                                                        #`((#,(->syntax
+                                                               (make-%wrap-name
+                                                                (or itype iname)))
                                                             name*)))
                                                        ((equal? atype "array")
                                                         #`((wrap-wl-array name*)))))))
-- 
